module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalDoublePoints.Homogenization
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.IdealFactorization

/-!
# The affine chart of the blowup of a rational double point

Section 54.12 of the source identifies the exceptional curve of the blowup of a rational double
point through the affine chart `A' = A[𝔪/x₁]` at a good coordinate `x₁`, by the isomorphism

`A[𝔪/x₁]/x₁·A[𝔪/x₁] ≅ κ[y₂, y₃]/(q(1, y₂, y₃))`.

The right hand side is `AlgebraicGeometry.map_dehomogenizeFirst_gradedRelationIdeal_eq_span` of
`RationalDoublePoints/FormPolynomial.lean`: the image of the homogeneous relation ideal under
dehomogenization at the first variable is generated by `q(1, y₂, y₃)`. This file provides the
left hand side, in two steps.

First, `A'` is generated over `A` by the three fractions `yᵢ = xᵢ/x₁`, of which `y₁ = 1`: by
definition `A'` is generated by all the fractions `y/x₁` with `y ∈ 𝔪`, and writing `y` in terms
of the generators `x₁, x₂, x₃` of `𝔪` expresses `y/x₁` as an `A`-combination of the `yᵢ`.

Second, `𝔪A' = x₁A'`, so `A'/x₁A'` is a `κ`-algebra, and it is generated over `κ` by `ȳ₂, ȳ₃`.
That gives a surjection `Φ : κ[y₂, y₃] ↠ A'/x₁A'`, and its kernel is the image of the relation
ideal. The inclusion `⊇` is formal: a homogeneous relation `P` of degree `n` with homogeneous
lift `Q` has `Q(x₁, x₂, x₃) ∈ 𝔪ⁿ⁺¹`, and the value of `Φ` on the dehomogenization of `P` is the
class of the fraction `Q(x₁, x₂, x₃)/x₁ⁿ`, which dies in `A'/x₁A'`. The inclusion `⊆` is the
superficiality of a good coordinate,
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_pow_succ_of_mul_mem_pow_of_isGoodCoordinateForm`: an element of the kernel
is the dehomogenization of some homogeneous `P`, whose lift then satisfies
`x₁ᴹ·Q(x₁, x₂, x₃) ∈ 𝔪ⁿ⁺ᴹ⁺¹` for some `M`, and superficiality divides the `x₁ᴹ` away to leave
`Q(x₁, x₂, x₃) ∈ 𝔪ⁿ⁺¹`, i.e. `P` is a relation.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.chartExceptionalQuotient`: the quotient `R[I/a]/a·R[I/a]`, the coordinate
  ring of the exceptional divisor on the chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.chartResidue`: the residue field acting on `A[𝔪/x₁]/x₁·A[𝔪/x₁]`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.chartPresentation`: **the surjection `κ[y₂, y₃] → A[𝔪/x₁]/x₁·A[𝔪/x₁]`**
  sending `yₚ` to the class of `xₚ/x₁`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.chartQuotientEquiv` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.chartQuotientEquivQuadric`: the identification itself, in general and for a
  rational double point at a good coordinate.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.adjoin_range_chartFraction_eq` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.adjoin_range_chartFraction_eq_top`: **`A[𝔪/x₁]` is generated over `A` by
  the fractions `xᵢ/x₁`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.aeval_chartFraction_eq_fraction`: a homogeneous `Q` of degree `n` evaluated
  at the fractions `xᵢ/x₁` is the single fraction `Q(x₁, x₂, x₃)/x₁ⁿ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.fraction_mem_span_singleton_of_mem_pow_succ` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_pow_succ_of_fraction_mem_span_singleton`: for `v ∈ 𝔪ⁿ` the fraction
  `v/x₁ⁿ` lies in `x₁A'` exactly when `v ∈ 𝔪ⁿ⁺¹`, the second direction for a superficial `x₁`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.chartPresentation_surjective`: **the chart quotient is generated by `ȳ₂`
  and `ȳ₃` over the residue field.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_chartPresentation`: **the kernel is the dehomogenized relation ideal.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_chartPresentation_eq_span`: **the left hand side of the chart
  identification**, with the kernel generated by
  `q(1, y₂, y₃) = ā₁₁ + ā₁₂y₂ + ā₁₃y₃ + ā₂₂y₂² + ā₂₃y₂y₃ + ā₃₃y₃²`, the polynomial the Claim of
  Section 54.12 is stated with.

## Implementation notes

The chart is `affineBlowupAlgebra (maximalIdeal A) (x 0) S` for an abstract localization `S` of
`A` away from `x₁`, the subalgebra model of `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Defs.lean`, which is
the model `AlgebraicGeometry.chartFraction` of `RationalDoublePoints/QuadraticForm.lean` already
speaks about. The fractions `v/x₁ⁿ` for `v ∈ 𝔪ⁿ` are `affineBlowupAlgebra.fraction`, and
`𝔪A' = x₁A'` is `affineBlowupAlgebra.map_ideal_eq_span_singleton`.

The presentation is a `RingHom` out of `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) (ResidueField A)` built with
`MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom` rather than an `AlgHom`, so that no `Algebra (ResidueField A)` instance
has to be installed on the quotient in order to state the results; the residue field acts
through `AlgebraicGeometry.chartResidue`, which is the first argument of the `eval₂Hom`.

That every element of `A'` becomes the image of an element of `𝔪ᵏ` after multiplication by
`x₁ᵏ` is proved here, by induction over the generators of the subalgebra
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_pow_mul_eq_algebraMap`). It is what converts membership of a fraction
in `x₁A'` into the divisibility statement `x₁ᴹ·v ∈ 𝔪ⁿ⁺ᴹ⁺¹` that superficiality consumes.

## Faithfulness: no `@[stacks]` attribute

Nothing here is tagged. The results carry the dimension formula
`dim_κ(𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹) = 2n + 1` in a binder `hdim`, exactly as their neighbours in
`RationalDoublePoints/GradedRelations.lean` and `RationalDoublePoints/FormPolynomial.lean` do;
that formula is proved nowhere in this development — the source derives it by Riemann–Roch on
the exceptional curve — so attaching a tag would register a conditional statement. The general
results `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_chartPresentation` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.chartQuotientEquiv` instead carry superficiality of `x₁` in a binder `hsup`,
which is a hypothesis the source's good-coordinate assumption supplies and which
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_pow_succ_of_mul_mem_pow_of_isGoodCoordinateForm` discharges under the
same `hdim`.

Tag 0BGE is registered in `RationalDoublePoints/ResolutionStages.lean`; this file is one of its
owed steps, not the whole of it.

